Data and methodology
Crime records come from Boston Police Department public data for 2025. This analysis keeps only the major crime categories used for the project, rather than treating every police response as a crime. Duplicate incident numbers are removed when calculating neighborhood and monthly totals.
Neighborhood boundaries and population estimates come from Boston GIS data. The population-adjusted measure is calculated as:
\[
\text{Crime Rate per 1,000}
=
\frac{\text{Unique Major Reported Crime Incidents}}
{\text{Neighborhood Population}}
\times 1000
\]
